From: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: avoid MPC pipe split on Apple Navi 14

While the Navi 14 of the MacBookPro16,1 drives the built-in 3072x1920
panel, UCLK stays at its top level and the board idles at about 15 W.
DML picks two MPC combined pipes for the panel. With the split the
surface uses an 8 line swath, and the 55 line vblank of the native
timing leaves too few lines for prefetch after the DRAM clock change
wait. DML then reports no DRAM clock change support and DC holds the
UCLK hard minimum at the top level.

The macOS driver sets DalPipeSplitPolicy to 1 on these GPUs and drives
the panel from one pipe at the native timing, with UCLK at its lowest
level at idle. Apply the same policy as dcdebugmask=0x1 on Apple Navi
14 boards. Leave the 5K iMacs out, nothing shows the same problem there.

Reported with dcdebugmask=0x1 on a MacBookPro16,1 5300M with the VBIOS
trained UCLK levels: one HUBP for the panel, UCLK at 95 MHz for 92 % of
a 45 minute desktop soak, board power 5.5 W instead of about 15 W, no
underflow.

Signed-off-by: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
@@ -2221,7 +2221,18 @@ static int amdgpu_dm_init(struct amdgpu_device *adev)
 		goto error;
 	}
 
-	if (amdgpu_dc_debug_mask & DC_DISABLE_PIPE_SPLIT) {
+	/*
+	 * On the 3072x1920 panel of the MacBookPro16,1 the MPC split leaves
+	 * too few vblank lines for prefetch, so DML reports no DRAM clock
+	 * change support and UCLK stays at its top level. The macOS driver
+	 * sets DalPipeSplitPolicy to 1 on these GPUs and drives the panel
+	 * from one pipe. The 5K iMacs are left out, nothing shows the same
+	 * problem there.
+	 */
+	if ((amdgpu_dc_debug_mask & DC_DISABLE_PIPE_SPLIT) ||
+	    (adev->asic_type == CHIP_NAVI14 &&
+	     adev->pdev->subsystem_vendor == PCI_VENDOR_ID_APPLE &&
+	     !adev->dm.imac5K_support)) {
 		adev->dm.dc->debug.force_single_disp_pipe_split = false;
 		adev->dm.dc->debug.pipe_split_policy = MPC_SPLIT_AVOID;
 	}
